<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<GameProfile xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <GamePath />
  <GamePath2 />
  <TestMenuParameter />
  <TestMenuIsExecutable>false</TestMenuIsExecutable>
  <ExtraParameters />
  <EmulationProfile>TeknoModel3</EmulationProfile>
  <GameProfileRevision>7</GameProfileRevision>
  <HasSeparateTestMode>false</HasSeparateTestMode>
  <EmulatorType>TeknoModel3</EmulatorType>
  <Is64Bit>true</Is64Bit>
  <ExecutableName>spikeofe.zip</ExecutableName>
  <HasTwoExecutables>false</HasTwoExecutables>
  <Patreon>true</Patreon>
  <DevOnly>false</DevOnly>
  <HasTpoSupport>true</HasTpoSupport>
  <ConfigValues>
    <FieldInformation>
      <CategoryName>General</CategoryName>
      <FieldName>Outputs</FieldName>
      <FieldValue>Windows Outputs</FieldValue>
      <FieldType>Dropdown</FieldType>
      <FieldOptions>
        <string>Windows Outputs</string>
        <string>Network Outputs</string>
      </FieldOptions>
      <Hint>Choose how game outputs are sent. Select Network Outputs to configure its settings.</Hint>
    </FieldInformation>
    <FieldInformation>
      <CategoryName>General</CategoryName>
      <FieldName>Input API</FieldName>
      <FieldValue>DirectInput</FieldValue>
      <FieldType>Dropdown</FieldType>
      <FieldOptions>
        <string>DirectInput</string>
        <string>XInput</string>
        <string>RawInput</string>
      </FieldOptions>
    </FieldInformation>
    <FieldInformation>
      <CategoryName>General</CategoryName>
      <FieldName>Region</FieldName>
      <FieldValue>Default</FieldValue>
      <FieldType>Dropdown</FieldType>
      <FieldOptions>
        <string>Default</string>
        <string>Japan</string>
        <string>USA</string>
        <string>Export</string>
        <string>Australia</string>
        <string>Korea</string>
      </FieldOptions>
      <Hint>Country saved in the game's own test-menu settings. It sets the language where the game has one (Japan shows Japanese text; Export or USA show English), the warning and rating screens, and regional attract. Default keeps the country already saved. Only this setting changes; calibration, bookkeeping and other test-menu settings are kept.</Hint>
    </FieldInformation>
    <FieldInformation>
      <CategoryName>Video</CategoryName>
      <FieldName>DisplayMode</FieldName>
      <FieldValue>Fullscreen</FieldValue>
      <FieldType>Dropdown</FieldType>
      <FieldOptions>
        <string>Windowed</string>
        <string>Fullscreen</string>
      </FieldOptions>
    </FieldInformation>
    <FieldInformation>
      <CategoryName>Video</CategoryName>
      <FieldName>Internal Resolution</FieldName>
      <FieldValue>4</FieldValue>
      <FieldType>Dropdown</FieldType>
      <FieldOptions>
        <string>1</string>
        <string>2</string>
        <string>4</string>
        <string>8</string>
      </FieldOptions>
    </FieldInformation>
    <FieldInformation>
      <CategoryName>Video</CategoryName>
      <FieldName>Presentation Filter</FieldName>
      <FieldValue>linear</FieldValue>
      <FieldType>Dropdown</FieldType>
      <FieldOptions>
        <string>nearest</string>
        <string>linear</string>
        <string>bicubic</string>
        <string>lanczos</string>
        <string>ssaa</string>
      </FieldOptions>
    </FieldInformation>
    <FieldInformation>
      <CategoryName>Video</CategoryName>
      <FieldName>VSync</FieldName>
      <FieldValue>On (recommended)</FieldValue>
      <FieldType>Dropdown</FieldType>
      <FieldOptions>
        <string>On (recommended)</string>
        <string>G-Sync / FreeSync monitor</string>
        <string>Off (may tear)</string>
      </FieldOptions>
      <Hint>How each finished frame reaches your monitor. On (recommended): no tearing; each frame appears at the monitor's next refresh. Best for ordinary 60 Hz and high-refresh monitors. G-Sync / FreeSync monitor: choose this only if variable refresh is enabled in your graphics driver, and play in Fullscreen. The monitor then refreshes exactly when each frame is ready (57.5 times a second, like the arcade), so there's no tearing, no stutter and no waiting for a refresh. Off (may tear): frames appear the instant they're ready. This is a few milliseconds quicker than On, but shows tearing lines on monitors without G-Sync/FreeSync. Desktop only; ignored in VR.</Hint>
    </FieldInformation>
    <FieldInformation>
      <CategoryName>Audio</CategoryName>
      <FieldName>Mute Audio</FieldName>
      <FieldValue>0</FieldValue>
      <FieldType>Bool</FieldType>
    </FieldInformation>
    <FieldInformation>
      <CategoryName>Video</CategoryName>
      <FieldName>Stretch to Fullscreen</FieldName>
      <FieldValue>0</FieldValue>
      <FieldType>Bool</FieldType>
      <Hint>Fill the entire display area. Off preserves the cabinet 4:3 aspect ratio.</Hint>
    </FieldInformation>
    <FieldInformation>
      <CategoryName>Video</CategoryName>
      <FieldName>Widescreen</FieldName>
      <FieldValue>0</FieldValue>
      <FieldType>Bool</FieldType>
      <Hint>16:9 view: the 3D scene is rendered wider while the HUD and menus keep their original 4:3 layout. Desktop only; ignored when VR is enabled.</Hint>
    </FieldInformation>
    <FieldInformation>
      <CategoryName>Video</CategoryName>
      <FieldName>Use Bezel</FieldName>
      <FieldValue>0</FieldValue>
      <FieldType>Bool</FieldType>
      <Hint>Load TeknoModel3/bezels/ROMSET.png, falling back to default.png. PNG alpha defines the game opening.</Hint>
    </FieldInformation>
    <FieldInformation>
      <CategoryName>Video</CategoryName>
      <FieldName>CRT Shader</FieldName>
      <FieldValue>None</FieldValue>
      <FieldType>Dropdown</FieldType>
      <FieldOptions>
        <string>None</string>
        <string>Lottes</string>
        <string>Lottes Downsample</string>
      </FieldOptions>
      <Hint>Lottes retains enhanced resolution; Lottes Downsample resolves to native CRT pixels first.</Hint>
    </FieldInformation>
    <FieldInformation>
      <CategoryName>Network</CategoryName>
      <FieldName>Enable LAN</FieldName>
      <FieldValue>0</FieldValue>
      <FieldType>Bool</FieldType>
      <Hint>Viper-style local multicast; no relay process or host address. The game's own link settings follow Cabinet Number and Cabinet Count.</Hint>
    </FieldInformation>
    <FieldInformation>
      <CategoryName>Network</CategoryName>
      <FieldName>Set Game Link Settings</FieldName>
      <FieldValue>1</FieldValue>
      <FieldType>Bool</FieldType>
      <Hint>Sets the link options in the game's test menu for you: master or slave and the car or cabinet number from Cabinet Number when LAN or TPOnline is used, and standalone (link off) otherwise, so the game can always be played alone. Turn off to keep the settings made in the game's test menu.</Hint>
    </FieldInformation>
    <FieldInformation>
      <CategoryName>Network</CategoryName>
      <FieldName>Network Port</FieldName>
      <FieldValue>42003</FieldValue>
      <FieldType>Text</FieldType>
      <Hint>Use the same UDP port on every cabinet, from 1 to 65535.</Hint>
    </FieldInformation>
    <FieldInformation>
      <CategoryName>Network</CategoryName>
      <FieldName>Cabinet Number</FieldName>
      <FieldValue>1</FieldValue>
      <FieldType>Dropdown</FieldType>
      <FieldOptions>
        <string>1</string>
        <string>2</string>
        <string>3</string>
        <string>4</string>
      </FieldOptions>
      <Hint>Unique number from 1 to Cabinet Count. Cabinet 1 is master; the others are slaves. This game links up to 4 cabinets.</Hint>
    </FieldInformation>
    <FieldInformation>
      <CategoryName>Network</CategoryName>
      <FieldName>Cabinet Count</FieldName>
      <FieldValue>2</FieldValue>
      <FieldType>Dropdown</FieldType>
      <FieldOptions>
        <string>2</string>
        <string>3</string>
        <string>4</string>
      </FieldOptions>
      <Hint>Same count on every cabinet, up to 4 for this game. All cabinets must be present before the ring starts.</Hint>
    </FieldInformation>
    <FieldInformation>
      <CategoryName>Network</CategoryName>
      <FieldName>Network Interface</FieldName>
      <FieldValue>auto</FieldValue>
      <FieldType>Text</FieldType>
      <Hint>auto or the local IPv4 address of the LAN adapter.</Hint>
    </FieldInformation>
    <FieldInformation>
      <CategoryName>Network</CategoryName>
      <FieldName>Network Diagnostics</FieldName>
      <FieldValue>1</FieldValue>
      <FieldType>Bool</FieldType>
      <Hint>Print LAN or TPOnline peer and frame statistics every five seconds. TPO lobby launches automatically use direct peers and override the LAN settings.</Hint>
    </FieldInformation>
    <FieldInformation>
      <CategoryName>VR</CategoryName>
      <FieldName>Enable VR</FieldName>
      <FieldValue>0</FieldValue>
      <FieldType>Bool</FieldType>
      <Hint>Present the game through OpenXR with geometric stereo on a virtual cabinet screen. The desktop window remains available as a spectator view.</Hint>
    </FieldInformation>
    <FieldInformation>
      <CategoryName>VR</CategoryName>
      <FieldName>Use VR Controls</FieldName>
      <FieldValue>1</FieldValue>
      <FieldType>Bool</FieldType>
      <Hint>When VR is enabled, use the OpenXR headset controllers. Turn this off to keep using TPUI bindings in VR. Hold controller Menu for VR settings; a short Menu press is Test.</Hint>
    </FieldInformation>
    <FieldInformation>
      <CategoryName>VR</CategoryName>
      <FieldName>VR Depth</FieldName>
      <FieldValue>150</FieldValue>
      <FieldType>Slider</FieldType>
      <FieldMin>100</FieldMin>
      <FieldMax>200</FieldMax>
      <FieldOptions />
      <FieldStep>5</FieldStep>
      <Hint>Adjust OpenXR stereo depth from 100% to 200%. Only used when VR is enabled.</Hint>
    </FieldInformation>
  </ConfigValues>
